    {
      "n": 20,
      "kind": "content",
      "title": "Smoothing Approaches",
      "text": "Smoothing Approaches\nWhen we forecast using historical data, the data contain two things: an underlying pattern and random fluctuations.\nTrend forecasting → captures the underlying pattern.\nIf we fit a trend line, we are imposing a particular mathematical pattern on the data.\nBut perhaps we don't want to assume that the underlying relationship is necessarily linear or quadratic.\nSo,\nMoving Average → Smooth the data by averaging recent observations.",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "When we forecast using historical data, the data contain two things: an underlying pattern and random fluctuations."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Trend forecasting → captures the underlying pattern."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "If we fit a trend line, we are imposing a particular mathematical pattern on the data."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "But perhaps we don't want to assume that the underlying relationship is necessarily linear or quadratic."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "So,"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Moving Average → Smooth the data by averaging recent observations."
        }
      ],
      "tables": [],
      "notes": "",
      "charts": [],
      "visual_text": "",
